The time complexity of this solution is O(n), where n is the length of the input string s. This is because we iterate through the string once to create the res list and then iterate through the res list once to join the characters into a string.

The space complexity of this solution is O(n), where n is the length of the input string s. This is because we create a new list res of the same length as the input string to store the characters in the correct order.

## Conclusion

This solution is efficient and easy to understand. It uses a simple approach to create a new list with the characters in the correct order and then joins the characters into a string. This solution is suitable for small to medium-sized strings.

