# coding-problem-solutions
This repository contains solutions to various coding problems. The solutions are written in Java and are designed to be efficient and optimized.

## Table of Contents
- [Introduction](#introduction)
- [Getting Started](#getting-started)
- [Contributing](#contributing)
- [License](#license)

## Introduction
This repository serves as a collection of coding problem solutions. Each solution is carefully crafted to provide an efficient and optimized approach to solving the given problem. The solutions are written in Java and are designed to be easy to understand and implement.

## Getting Started
To get started with the coding problem solutions, follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository to your local machine using the following command:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/coding-problem-solutions.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the directory containing the solutions:
   ```
   cd coding-problem-solutions
   ```

3. Explore the different solution files in the repository. Each file contains a solution to a specific coding problem.

4. Read the code and understand the approach used to solve the problem.

5. If you want to contribute to the repository, follow the instructions in the [Contributing](#contributing) section.

## Contributing
We welcome contributions from the community to improve and expand the collection of coding problem solutions. To contribute, follow these steps:

1. Fork the repository to your own GitHub account.

2. Clone the forked repository to your local machine:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/coding-problem-solutions.git
   ```

3. Create a new branch for your contribution:
   ```
   git checkout -b your-branch-name
   ```

4. Make the necessary changes to the code and add your solution to the repository.

5. Commit your changes with a descriptive commit message:
   ```
   git commit -m "Add solution for problem XYZ"
   ```

6. Push your changes to your forked repository:
   ```
   git push origin your-branch-name
   ```

7. Create a pull request from your forked repository to the original repository.

8. Wait for the maintainers to review and merge your pull request.

## License
The coding problem solutions in this repository are licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE). You are free to use, modify, and distribute the solutions as per the terms of the license.

---

Feel free to reach out if you have any questions or need further assistance. Happy coding!
