Output: 3

## Problem 4: Minimum Number of Platforms Required

### Description
You are given an array of arrival and departure times of trains at a railway station. Your task is to find the minimum number of platforms required to handle all the trains without any overlap.

### Solution
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.io.*;

public class MinimumPlatformsRequired {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws NumberFormatException, IOException {
        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));
        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine());
        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());
        int[] arr = new int[n];
        int[] dep = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            arr[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());
            dep[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());
        }
        Arrays.sort(arr);
        Arrays.sort(dep);
        int platforms = 1;
        int maxPlatforms = 1;
        int i = 1, j = 0;
        while (i < n && j < n) {
            if (arr[i] <= dep[j]) {
                platforms++;
                i++;
            } else {
                platforms--;
                j++;
            }
            if (platforms > maxPlatforms)
                maxPlatforms = platforms;
        }
        System.out.println(maxPlatforms);
    }
}
```

