# Codechef
This repository contains solutions to various coding problems on Codechef. The solutions are written in Java and are optimized for execution efficiency and memory usage.

## Problem 1: [Codechef](https://www.codechef.com/problems/CHFNSWPS)
### Problem Statement
You are given an array of integers. You need to find the number of ways to swap two elements in the array such that the sum of the elements in the array is maximized.

### Solution
The solution to this problem is implemented in the `Codechef` class. The `main` method takes input from the user, processes it, and prints the result.

### Code
```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Codechef {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = input.nextInt();
        int[] arr = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            arr[i] = input.nextInt();
        }

        int max = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                int sum = arr[i] + arr[j];
                if (sum > max) {
                    max = sum;
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println(max);
    }
}
```

