# coding-problem-solutions
This repository contains solutions to various coding problems. The solutions are provided in different programming languages, including Java, Python, C++, and JavaScript. Each solution is accompanied by a detailed explanation and test cases to ensure its correctness.

## Table of Contents
- [Introduction](#introduction)
- [Getting Started](#getting-started)
- [Contributing](#contributing)
- [License](#license)

## Introduction
Coding problems are an essential part of the software development process. They help developers improve their problem-solving skills, coding abilities, and understanding of various programming concepts. This repository aims to provide a collection of coding problem solutions that can be used as a reference or a learning resource for developers.

## Getting Started
To get started with the coding problem solutions in this repository, follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository to your local machine using the following command:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/coding-problem-solutions.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the directory containing the solutions you are interested in.

3. Review the code and test cases provided for each solution.

4. Run the test cases to ensure the solutions work as expected.

5. If you find any issues or have suggestions for improvement, feel free to contribute to the repository.

## Contributing
Contributions to this repository are welcome! If you have a solution to a coding problem that you would like to share, please follow these guidelines:

1. Fork the repository and create a new branch for your solution.

2. Write your solution in the appropriate programming language and ensure it passes the provided test cases.

3. Add a detailed explanation of your solution and any relevant information.

4. Commit your changes and push them to your forked repository.

5. Submit a pull request to the main repository, explaining the changes you made and why they are valuable.

## License
This repository is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE). Feel free to use the solutions provided here for your own projects or learning purposes. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don't hesitate to contact me.

Thank you for your interest in this repository! I hope you find the coding problem solutions helpful in your coding journey.
